       The complex character type cccchhaarr__tt can store more than one wide charac‐
       ter (wwcchhaarr__tt).  The X/Open Curses description  does  not  mention  this
       possibility, describing only the cases where _w_c_h is a spacing character
       or a non-spacing character.

       This implementation assumes that _w_c_h is constructed using sseettcccchhaarr(3X),
       and in turn that the result

       •   contains at most one spacing character in the beginning of its list
           of wide characters, and zero or more non-spacing characters or

       •   may hold one non-spacing character.

       In the latter case, _n_c_u_r_s_e_s adds the non-spacing character to  the  ac‐
       tive (base) spacing character.

